1
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:06,680
- <i>Just act natural at school, okay?</i>
- Putter!

2
00:00:07,200 --> 00:00:08,160
<i>That damage is insane.</i>

3
00:00:08,240 --> 00:00:09,640
<i>How am I supposed to handle it?</i>

4
00:00:09,720 --> 00:00:11,520
- Am I cute?
- Yeah.

5
00:00:11,600 --> 00:00:14,160
<i>What's with you? You're just too cute.</i>

6
00:00:15,600 --> 00:00:17,680
<i>You and Putter…</i>
<i>you're really not together, right?</i>

7
00:00:17,760 --> 00:00:19,160
<i>Are you doubting me?</i>

8
00:00:20,080 --> 00:00:21,240
<i>Then why did you lie to me?</i>

9
00:00:21,320 --> 00:00:22,920
<i>About going to Song Wat with Putter.</i>

10
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:24,880
<i>If you don't want me</i>
<i>as your friend anymore,</i>

11
00:00:24,960 --> 00:00:26,760
then just say it, damn it!

12
00:00:26,840 --> 00:00:28,800
<i>Holy shit, Lee! Have you seen this?</i>

13
00:00:28,880 --> 00:00:30,640
<i>The Brain Drain gang found</i>
<i>Putter's alt account,</i>

14
00:00:30,720 --> 00:00:33,080
<i>and it looks like he likes Indy too.</i>

15
00:00:35,640 --> 00:00:37,120
- I've got your delivery.
- How much is it?

16
00:00:37,200 --> 00:00:38,360
That'll be 80 baht.

17
00:00:38,440 --> 00:00:39,480
- The transfer's complete.
- Got it.

18
00:00:39,560 --> 00:00:41,240
- Thank you very much.
- Thank you.

19
00:00:41,320 --> 00:00:42,960
- Enjoy your meal.
- Thank you.

20
00:00:54,360 --> 00:00:56,120
Hey, Ter.

21
00:00:56,200 --> 00:00:57,960
- Hey, Ter.
- Ter.

22
00:00:59,200 --> 00:01:01,760
- Ter.
- Putter.

23
00:01:01,840 --> 00:01:02,920
You're so sneaky.

24
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:04,599
You didn't tell us at all.

25
00:01:04,680 --> 00:01:05,960
Yeah.

26
00:01:06,480 --> 00:01:09,720
I knew it. I was wondering why he asked me
what perfume you wore that day.

27
00:01:11,200 --> 00:01:12,480
What's with you guys?

28
00:01:14,200 --> 00:01:15,400
You like Indy, don't you?

29
00:01:18,600 --> 00:01:20,440
Just admit it already.

30
00:01:20,520 --> 00:01:22,560
- Gotcha!
- Busted!

31
00:01:22,640 --> 00:01:24,040
Come on, tell me.

32
00:01:24,120 --> 00:01:25,280
Where did you hear that?

33
00:01:26,360 --> 00:01:27,680
From your alt account.

34
00:01:28,600 --> 00:01:29,480
Here.

35
00:01:30,680 --> 00:01:31,800
If you like him, just ask him out.

36
00:01:31,880 --> 00:01:32,880
What are you waiting for?

37
00:01:32,960 --> 00:01:34,320
- Don't be scared.
- Mr. President.

38
00:01:35,280 --> 00:01:36,520
I can, right?

39
00:01:36,600 --> 00:01:38,040
- Hey.
- Give me the go-ahead.

40
00:01:38,120 --> 00:01:40,360
I knew it. When you said you had a crush,

41
00:01:40,440 --> 00:01:42,000
you meant Indy, didn't you?

42
00:01:42,600 --> 00:01:43,440
Right?

43
00:01:45,800 --> 00:01:46,760
Of course.

44
00:01:46,840 --> 00:01:48,840
Why didn't you tell us?

45
00:02:36,480 --> 00:02:39,760
Lee, just hear me out first. Lee!

46
00:02:39,840 --> 00:02:42,080
I'm listening. Go ahead and explain.

47
00:02:42,160 --> 00:02:43,440
It's true, isn't it?

48
00:02:45,200 --> 00:02:46,240
It used to be.

49
00:02:48,480 --> 00:02:50,960
<i>I like Indie music too.</i>

50
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:53,240
How Indie are we talking?

51
00:02:53,840 --> 00:02:54,920
I listen to all kinds.

52
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:56,760
Could you guys keep it down a little?

53
00:02:56,840 --> 00:02:59,520
<i>Long story short, we're in the same year.</i>

54
00:02:59,600 --> 00:03:02,280
I'm going to find out
who you have a crush on.

55
00:03:05,800 --> 00:03:07,160
But I don't like him anymore.

56
00:03:07,680 --> 00:03:10,600
I mean… You got over him that fast?

57
00:03:12,840 --> 00:03:13,920
Or…

58
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:15,560
Are you using me as Indy's replacement?

59
00:03:15,640 --> 00:03:17,840
No. I really do like you.

60
00:03:21,120 --> 00:03:23,880
Lee. Lee.

61
00:03:24,840 --> 00:03:26,080
Just hear me out first.

62
00:03:28,280 --> 00:03:29,640
I think we should break up.

63
00:03:29,720 --> 00:03:32,920
I can't date someone who used to
have a crush on my best friend.

64
00:05:25,640 --> 00:05:27,120
Come on, let's take some pictures.

65
00:05:27,200 --> 00:05:28,840
No way. I'm not taking any.

66
00:05:28,920 --> 00:05:30,160
Come on.

67
00:05:56,040 --> 00:05:57,120
Look! This plushie is so cute.

68
00:05:58,400 --> 00:05:59,320
It's for you.

69
00:05:59,400 --> 00:06:01,920
This one's for you. Now we're even.

70
00:06:15,720 --> 00:06:17,040
Here. I got this for you.

71
00:06:27,920 --> 00:06:28,760
Shit.

72
00:06:28,840 --> 00:06:30,280
Proud.

73
00:06:32,440 --> 00:06:33,400
Indy.

74
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:38,840
PUTTER DEFINITELY LIKES INDY

75
00:06:38,920 --> 00:06:41,160
<i>Putter definitely likes Indy.</i>

76
00:06:41,240 --> 00:06:43,720
<i>So it's not Lee and Putter after all?</i>

77
00:06:43,800 --> 00:06:45,880
Wait, is this for real
or are they just stirring things up?

78
00:06:45,960 --> 00:06:49,400
The Brain Drain gang says
this really is Putter's account.

79
00:06:59,240 --> 00:07:00,200
Leo.

80
00:07:00,840 --> 00:07:03,480
Didn't you come to school
with Lee and Ter?

81
00:07:05,200 --> 00:07:06,320
Uh…

82
00:07:06,400 --> 00:07:08,720
Lee… I don't know what got him so upset.

83
00:07:08,800 --> 00:07:10,160
So Ter went after him.

84
00:07:10,240 --> 00:07:12,640
Hey, but we have practice today.

85
00:07:13,800 --> 00:07:15,040
I think…

86
00:07:17,000 --> 00:07:18,320
Let's just leave it for now.

87
00:07:18,920 --> 00:07:19,840
Trust me.

88
00:07:21,200 --> 00:07:24,520
I agree. I think we should
cancel practice today, Indy.

89
00:07:25,120 --> 00:07:28,160
Yeah… I'll go cancel
the room booking first.

90
00:08:10,560 --> 00:08:12,200
You should take a break.

91
00:08:14,560 --> 00:08:16,560
The more you force it,
the worse it'll get.

92
00:08:23,760 --> 00:08:24,720
Are you stressed?

93
00:08:26,520 --> 00:08:27,640
How could you tell?

94
00:08:32,600 --> 00:08:34,200
Your linework gave it away.

95
00:08:35,000 --> 00:08:36,000
It's shaky.

96
00:08:36,679 --> 00:08:38,559
You're usually much steadier than this.

97
00:08:47,040 --> 00:08:48,520
I'm fine.

98
00:08:48,600 --> 00:08:49,800
I'm just a little tired.

99
00:08:49,880 --> 00:08:52,000
I'll get some rest. I'll feel better soon.

100
00:08:52,960 --> 00:08:55,000
Go on, head home and get some rest.

101
00:08:55,080 --> 00:08:57,080
I'll save your attendance
credit this time.

102
00:09:00,320 --> 00:09:03,320
Hey, is LeeIth still taking the class?

103
00:09:03,400 --> 00:09:05,040
He already paid for the full course,

104
00:09:05,120 --> 00:09:06,480
but he hasn't shown up at all.

105
00:09:07,320 --> 00:09:08,400
I think…

106
00:09:09,360 --> 00:09:12,560
he… probably changed his mind.

107
00:10:47,800 --> 00:10:48,760
I'm back!

108
00:10:49,280 --> 00:10:50,600
<i>Hey. Putter's here!</i>

109
00:10:52,160 --> 00:10:54,160
<i>The team we're scrimming against</i>
<i>are pretty good.</i>

110
00:10:54,240 --> 00:10:56,720
<i>We're all here now, right?</i>

111
00:10:56,800 --> 00:10:59,320
<i>Let's take it easy today, okay?</i>

112
00:11:07,400 --> 00:11:09,080
THIS IS NO ONE ELSE'S BUSINESS

113
00:11:09,160 --> 00:11:11,320
<i>This is no one else's business.</i>

114
00:11:16,880 --> 00:11:18,320
DEACTIVATE YOUR ACCOUNT

115
00:11:18,400 --> 00:11:19,280
DEACTIVATE

116
00:11:19,360 --> 00:11:20,440
<i>Are you guys ready?</i>

117
00:11:21,680 --> 00:11:24,000
Come on, everyone. Let's do this!

118
00:11:31,800 --> 00:11:35,480
INDY

119
00:11:47,600 --> 00:11:50,200
Indy, you've called a hundred times.
Stop calling.

120
00:11:53,920 --> 00:11:55,720
Both Ter and Lee…

121
00:11:55,800 --> 00:11:57,920
Damn, they've both disappeared.

122
00:11:58,000 --> 00:11:59,160
What the hell's going on with them?

123
00:11:59,240 --> 00:12:01,320
Maybe they're sick.

124
00:12:01,400 --> 00:12:06,040
Hey, I think…
it might be about Putter's alt account.

125
00:12:08,400 --> 00:12:09,400
What do you mean?

126
00:12:10,680 --> 00:12:13,800
Well…

127
00:12:17,200 --> 00:12:19,520
Well…

128
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:29,120
Leo.

129
00:12:31,400 --> 00:12:33,320
Do you have something to say?

130
00:12:33,400 --> 00:12:34,960
Well…

131
00:12:35,720 --> 00:12:37,960
You know where they went, don't you?

132
00:12:51,560 --> 00:12:53,240
Well…

133
00:12:53,880 --> 00:12:59,120
I'm not really sure, but I think…

134
00:12:59,880 --> 00:13:01,040
Lee.

135
00:13:01,120 --> 00:13:03,400
<i>That day, Neo told me to go after them.</i>

136
00:13:03,480 --> 00:13:05,360
- <i>They were worried they'd start fighting.</i>
- Lee.

137
00:13:05,440 --> 00:13:06,840
Will you just hear me out?

138
00:13:06,920 --> 00:13:09,080
Let's break up.

139
00:13:09,160 --> 00:13:11,360
I can't date someone
who's in love with my best friend.

140
00:13:18,640 --> 00:13:19,800
Shit.

141
00:13:20,920 --> 00:13:22,360
When did they even start dating?

142
00:13:24,920 --> 00:13:26,280
Seriously, when did they get together?

143
00:13:26,360 --> 00:13:27,920
And they've already broken up?

144
00:13:28,960 --> 00:13:30,960
At first, I didn't believe it either.

145
00:13:31,040 --> 00:13:32,600
But after Leo told me,

146
00:13:32,680 --> 00:13:36,200
and with the way LeeIth
was acting all secretive,

147
00:13:36,280 --> 00:13:37,600
it all started to make sense.

148
00:13:37,680 --> 00:13:40,320
And… you weren't going to tell me?

149
00:13:40,400 --> 00:13:41,240
You traitorous twins.

150
00:13:42,040 --> 00:13:43,080
Uh…

151
00:13:43,600 --> 00:13:45,160
We had to respect our friends' privacy.

152
00:13:46,240 --> 00:13:48,160
I'm the only one who didn't know.

153
00:13:49,720 --> 00:13:52,160
He made the rules,
then broke them himself.

154
00:13:52,240 --> 00:13:53,720
That's my badass president.

155
00:13:54,320 --> 00:13:56,880
Maybe that's why he doesn't
want to face us.

156
00:13:58,160 --> 00:14:00,160
Why are you all gossiping here?

157
00:14:00,240 --> 00:14:01,560
Don't you have a club room?

158
00:14:01,640 --> 00:14:03,480
The club room isn't safe anymore.

159
00:14:03,560 --> 00:14:05,680
We can't let outsiders
find out about this.

160
00:14:07,880 --> 00:14:09,480
Then why am I allowed to know?

161
00:14:09,560 --> 00:14:11,280
You're not an outsider.

162
00:14:11,360 --> 00:14:12,880
I already consider you a friend.

163
00:14:12,960 --> 00:14:15,440
Besides, I know you already knew.

164
00:14:15,520 --> 00:14:18,280
I know nothing. I'm going back to sleep.

165
00:14:18,360 --> 00:14:20,400
Then let's get the plan started.

166
00:14:20,480 --> 00:14:22,160
Everyone, take out your phones.

167
00:14:25,520 --> 00:14:26,800
<i>I miss you guys.</i>

168
00:14:26,880 --> 00:14:27,880
I MISS YOU GUYS.

169
00:14:28,760 --> 00:14:30,280
<i>Yeah, Te.</i>

170
00:14:30,360 --> 00:14:31,640
<i>So what are we supposed to do?</i>

171
00:14:31,720 --> 00:14:33,880
<i>Exactly, Neo.</i>

172
00:14:36,320 --> 00:14:38,760
- What?
- Act natural.

173
00:14:40,760 --> 00:14:41,920
Come on, help me think.

174
00:14:45,920 --> 00:14:48,360
<i>Oh, shit. We have</i>
<i>an assignment to turn in.</i>

175
00:14:48,440 --> 00:14:50,600
Yeah, that's much more natural.

176
00:14:50,680 --> 00:14:51,840
<i>Then it's settled.</i>

177
00:14:51,920 --> 00:14:54,600
<i>Tomorrow at 4:30. At the club room.</i>

178
00:14:54,680 --> 00:14:56,440
<i>Let's get it done once and for all.</i>

179
00:14:57,560 --> 00:14:58,400
LET'S GET IT DONE ONCE AND FOR ALL.

180
00:15:02,600 --> 00:15:05,640
I think… we should make them
send a sticker.

181
00:15:05,720 --> 00:15:07,120
Otherwise, they'll just say
they didn't see it.

182
00:15:08,720 --> 00:15:10,640
Brilliant, my vice president.

183
00:15:11,800 --> 00:15:14,160
<i>If you've read it, send one sticker.</i>

184
00:15:14,240 --> 00:15:16,000
IF YOU'VE READ IT, SEND ONE STICKER.

185
00:15:20,120 --> 00:15:22,320
Damn it. Now it's obvious we set this up.

186
00:15:29,560 --> 00:15:30,960
One more.

187
00:15:31,040 --> 00:15:32,000
Come on, buddy.

188
00:15:32,080 --> 00:15:33,320
I've been so nervous I could barely pee.

189
00:15:34,960 --> 00:15:36,680
<i>Alright. See you then.</i>

190
00:15:38,240 --> 00:15:40,360
- So?
- Lee sounded tense as hell.

191
00:15:40,440 --> 00:15:41,800
He didn't even send a sticker.

192
00:15:41,880 --> 00:15:44,120
It's okay. At least he's coming.

193
00:15:44,200 --> 00:15:47,760
Our friendship-repair
mission won't be that hard after all.

194
00:15:50,080 --> 00:15:51,320
Awesome.

195
00:15:51,400 --> 00:15:53,240
Alright.

196
00:15:53,320 --> 00:15:55,520
"DON'T" DATE SOMEONE CLOSE TO YOU!

197
00:16:28,640 --> 00:16:31,360
I think… this one's pretty serious, guys.

198
00:16:34,720 --> 00:16:36,560
I think we should talk to them separately.

199
00:16:37,240 --> 00:16:39,000
Going as a group probably won't work.

200
00:16:58,840 --> 00:17:00,680
I know about you and Ter.

201
00:17:05,480 --> 00:17:07,040
How are you holding up? Are you okay?

202
00:17:09,040 --> 00:17:10,440
I don't know.

203
00:17:13,000 --> 00:17:15,040
Forget it. You wouldn't understand.

204
00:17:15,119 --> 00:17:16,240
Come on, asshole.

205
00:17:16,880 --> 00:17:18,119
Why do you never say anything?

206
00:17:18,200 --> 00:17:19,960
Because he likes you.

207
00:17:20,040 --> 00:17:21,319
He doesn't like me.

208
00:17:22,720 --> 00:17:23,920
Don't take it out on me.

209
00:17:24,000 --> 00:17:26,160
I even let it slide when you lied to me.

210
00:17:26,240 --> 00:17:27,839
But I can't let this slide.

211
00:17:36,800 --> 00:17:37,920
Guys, calm down.

212
00:17:38,000 --> 00:17:40,480
Weren't you the one who made that rule?

213
00:17:40,560 --> 00:17:42,080
And now you're the one breaking it.

214
00:17:42,160 --> 00:17:43,600
You even lied to your friends.

215
00:17:43,680 --> 00:17:45,120
Because the rule is ridiculous.

216
00:17:45,200 --> 00:17:47,680
Who can stop themselves
from falling for someone?

217
00:17:47,760 --> 00:17:50,160
But you made that rule,
so you shouldn't be breaking it.

218
00:17:50,240 --> 00:17:51,680
Especially you, Ter.

219
00:17:51,760 --> 00:17:53,840
You're the last person who should be
saying that, you loudmouth.

220
00:17:53,920 --> 00:17:56,400
Stop it!
It's my fault for making that rule.

221
00:17:56,480 --> 00:17:57,640
That's enough.

222
00:17:57,720 --> 00:17:59,280
I'm leaving this club.

223
00:17:59,360 --> 00:18:01,320
I never wanted to be
in this damn club anyway.

224
00:18:06,440 --> 00:18:08,240
- Hey, Ter!
- Ter!

225
00:18:08,320 --> 00:18:09,600
- Putter!
- Ter!

226
00:18:13,120 --> 00:18:14,640
That's enough, you assholes.

227
00:18:14,720 --> 00:18:15,840
You've gone too far.

228
00:18:16,720 --> 00:18:18,080
Just calm down.

229
00:18:18,160 --> 00:18:19,600
Aren't we friends in the end?

230
00:18:21,680 --> 00:18:24,280
Friends don't talk to each other
like this, asshole.

231
00:18:26,000 --> 00:18:28,760
Then stop being my friend.
I'm the asshole.

232
00:18:33,960 --> 00:18:34,880
Lee.

233
00:18:38,000 --> 00:18:42,160
"DON'T" DATE SOMEONE CLOSE TO YOU!

234
00:19:08,960 --> 00:19:11,000
It's weird without the guys around.

235
00:19:11,080 --> 00:19:12,000
Yeah, isn't it?

236
00:19:12,600 --> 00:19:14,120
Look.

237
00:19:14,200 --> 00:19:16,280
The table is so much quieter.

238
00:19:16,360 --> 00:19:17,960
Yeah.

239
00:19:18,040 --> 00:19:21,480
So… Was their fight really that bad?

240
00:19:22,160 --> 00:19:23,920
Yeah, it was pretty bad.

241
00:19:24,440 --> 00:19:26,480
So, have you talked to Ter?

242
00:19:26,560 --> 00:19:29,440
He's not answering my calls,
and he won't even reply to my messages.

243
00:19:35,280 --> 00:19:37,200
What's wrong with you?

244
00:19:39,280 --> 00:19:40,480
I feel guilty.

245
00:19:41,760 --> 00:19:42,800
Guilty about what?

246
00:19:44,040 --> 00:19:48,360
At first, I was totally fangirling
when I saw Putter's post on X.

247
00:19:49,080 --> 00:19:52,360
When people dug it up, I was excited too.

248
00:19:52,880 --> 00:19:56,760
But when I saw Putter feeling so awful,
I felt even more guilty.

249
00:19:57,360 --> 00:19:58,960
Yeah, exactly.

250
00:19:59,040 --> 00:20:02,160
Maybe the universe is trying
to teach you a lesson.

251
00:20:02,240 --> 00:20:04,680
Don't let the brain rot
consume you until you fall.

252
00:20:04,760 --> 00:20:08,160
Seriously. These days, once you fall,
you don't get back up.

253
00:20:08,240 --> 00:20:09,560
Ugh.

254
00:20:10,080 --> 00:20:12,080
I already feel bad enough.

255
00:20:12,160 --> 00:20:14,520
If you feel guilty,
then go apologize to Ter.

256
00:20:14,600 --> 00:20:16,600
You can wait until the timing feels right.

257
00:20:58,360 --> 00:20:59,320
Hey.

258
00:21:00,240 --> 00:21:01,360
Yeah?

259
00:21:04,320 --> 00:21:06,120
Speak, or I'm going back to watching TV.

260
00:21:07,160 --> 00:21:08,680
Reply to your aunt's message too.

261
00:21:09,520 --> 00:21:11,080
She wants to talk to you
about architecture tutoring.

262
00:21:13,120 --> 00:21:14,480
Okay. Thanks.

263
00:21:48,960 --> 00:21:50,520
Why won't he just get some sleep?

264
00:22:58,640 --> 00:23:00,360
Shit. I'm late.

265
00:23:08,680 --> 00:23:10,480
You have P.E. first period.

266
00:23:12,840 --> 00:23:13,800
Yeah.

267
00:23:14,320 --> 00:23:15,920
I bought two lunch boxes.

268
00:23:16,480 --> 00:23:17,960
Help yourself if you get hungry.

269
00:23:18,840 --> 00:23:20,400
In case you don't have time
to grab something.

270
00:23:28,360 --> 00:23:31,240
But if you don't eat it,
put it in the fridge.

271
00:23:59,240 --> 00:24:00,600
Damn it.

272
00:24:14,960 --> 00:24:18,200
I can only refund you 50%, LeeIth,
according to the school's policy.

273
00:24:18,280 --> 00:24:20,680
That's fine. I'll explain it to my mom.

274
00:24:23,400 --> 00:24:24,360
All set.

275
00:24:26,240 --> 00:24:29,040
So, which faculty did you
decide to switch to?

276
00:24:29,720 --> 00:24:31,880
Putter said you changed your mind.

277
00:24:34,560 --> 00:24:35,480
There he is.

278
00:24:43,120 --> 00:24:44,920
LeeIth came to request a refund.

279
00:24:47,880 --> 00:24:49,760
Yeah, it's good that you came to
process the refund.

280
00:24:50,800 --> 00:24:52,840
I'll get going now. Goodbye.

281
00:25:04,560 --> 00:25:06,560
If you need to vent,
you can always talk to me, Ter.

282
00:25:07,400 --> 00:25:08,400
Okay.

283
00:25:09,160 --> 00:25:11,680
And don't forget, today's
the sketch design submission.

284
00:25:12,520 --> 00:25:13,400
Okay.

285
00:26:42,120 --> 00:26:43,800
<i>Try not to take Grab so often.</i>

286
00:26:43,880 --> 00:26:46,320
<i>It's been charging my card nonstop.</i>

287
00:26:46,400 --> 00:26:48,640
<i>I know. I saw it.</i>

288
00:27:06,160 --> 00:27:08,040
<i>Is he stalking you again?</i>

289
00:27:11,480 --> 00:27:13,040
<i>I think Lee still has feelings for you.</i>

290
00:27:13,120 --> 00:27:14,520
<i>He's just putting on an act.</i>

291
00:27:17,200 --> 00:27:19,200
<i>So what's he going to do?</i>

292
00:27:20,400 --> 00:27:21,800
<i>Calm down.</i>

293
00:27:23,480 --> 00:27:24,880
<i>You defend him too much.</i>

294
00:27:24,960 --> 00:27:26,240
<i>Think you'll get back together?</i>

295
00:27:27,800 --> 00:27:29,880
<i>We should just stay friends.</i>

296
00:27:29,960 --> 00:27:31,280
<i>It's probably for the best.</i>

297
00:27:32,480 --> 00:27:35,360
<i>I respect whatever you decide.</i>

298
00:27:35,440 --> 00:27:37,160
<i>Put that energy into practice.</i>

299
00:27:37,240 --> 00:27:38,480
<i>I'll be cheering for you.</i>

300
00:28:11,280 --> 00:28:14,440
Let the sound waves work
through your body.

301
00:28:15,160 --> 00:28:18,880
And release the emotions
you've been holding onto

302
00:28:19,480 --> 00:28:21,680
through your breath.

303
00:28:23,040 --> 00:28:25,680
Take a deep breath in.

304
00:28:29,000 --> 00:28:32,080
And breathe out slowly.

305
00:28:41,400 --> 00:28:44,400
Take a deep breath in.

306
00:28:44,480 --> 00:28:47,000
And breathe out slowly.

307
00:28:58,560 --> 00:29:00,480
Take a deep breath in.

308
00:29:07,120 --> 00:29:08,360
That's a bit too intense.

309
00:29:08,440 --> 00:29:09,800
Okay, okay.

310
00:29:17,840 --> 00:29:18,880
That's funny.

311
00:29:28,800 --> 00:29:29,960
How did that feel?

312
00:29:31,960 --> 00:29:33,160
I feel pretty good.

313
00:29:34,480 --> 00:29:35,720
I figured you'd feel better.

314
00:29:35,800 --> 00:29:37,240
You let out quite a sigh.

315
00:29:37,760 --> 00:29:39,320
You probably got it all out.

316
00:29:40,840 --> 00:29:42,160
Why are you so irritated?

317
00:29:52,000 --> 00:29:53,480
I'm happy for you.

318
00:29:54,080 --> 00:29:56,040
I'm glad you finally let it out.

319
00:29:56,120 --> 00:29:58,240
I'll go make you some cocoa.

320
00:29:58,320 --> 00:29:59,840
- Make yourself at home.
- Yes, Mom.

321
00:29:59,920 --> 00:30:00,800
Okay.

322
00:30:13,520 --> 00:30:15,160
What are we going to do about Lee?

323
00:30:15,760 --> 00:30:17,000
Read the cards for me.

324
00:30:17,800 --> 00:30:19,320
No card readings for two months.

325
00:30:19,400 --> 00:30:20,520
Why?

326
00:30:21,040 --> 00:30:23,080
You're addicted to them.

327
00:30:27,680 --> 00:30:29,760
I think I'm more addicted to you,
fortune teller.

328
00:30:30,640 --> 00:30:33,120
I'm seeing you, and you want me
to go see someone else?

329
00:30:33,200 --> 00:30:34,880
Try living your own life.

330
00:30:34,960 --> 00:30:36,080
Otherwise, one day,

331
00:30:36,160 --> 00:30:38,200
you'll need to read the cards
before taking your first step.

332
00:30:38,280 --> 00:30:39,560
That'll make life difficult.

333
00:30:41,320 --> 00:30:42,440
Yeah.

334
00:30:42,520 --> 00:30:43,760
You've got a point.

335
00:30:44,520 --> 00:30:45,600
But it's hard.

336
00:30:46,200 --> 00:30:47,640
That's life.

337
00:30:47,720 --> 00:30:50,040
You never know what's going to happen.

338
00:30:50,560 --> 00:30:53,160
Even if the cards say so,
it doesn't mean it'll actually happen.

339
00:30:58,080 --> 00:30:59,280
You're pretty sharp.

340
00:30:59,840 --> 00:31:01,520
I got it all from my mom.

341
00:31:01,600 --> 00:31:02,800
I get it.

342
00:31:02,880 --> 00:31:04,080
You got your sharpness from your mom.

343
00:31:04,680 --> 00:31:06,000
You know, you're a lot like her.

344
00:31:06,080 --> 00:31:07,120
My face?

345
00:31:07,640 --> 00:31:08,880
Your vibe too.

346
00:31:08,960 --> 00:31:11,520
Like, I feel at ease around you.

347
00:31:13,440 --> 00:31:14,280
Can you say that again?

348
00:31:14,360 --> 00:31:15,240
I want to use it in the café's review.

349
00:31:15,320 --> 00:31:16,520
Sure.

350
00:31:22,360 --> 00:31:24,520
You're camera-shy for a Gen Z.

351
00:31:25,120 --> 00:31:26,040
Stop teasing me.

352
00:31:26,120 --> 00:31:29,240
Besides, no Gen Z
actually calls someone a "Gen Z."

353
00:31:29,320 --> 00:31:30,680
Only old people do.

354
00:31:40,080 --> 00:31:42,040
- So cute.
- So cute.

355
00:31:42,120 --> 00:31:43,240
Hey.

356
00:31:45,880 --> 00:31:48,800
Going on a date with the three of us…

357
00:31:48,880 --> 00:31:51,560
- You're okay with that, right?
- Sure. It's fun.

358
00:31:51,640 --> 00:31:52,800
Did you even ask me?

359
00:31:53,480 --> 00:31:55,600
- Hey, Summer.
- Wow.

360
00:31:55,680 --> 00:31:57,560
- So cute.
- It looks great on you.

361
00:31:57,640 --> 00:31:58,600
Really?

362
00:31:58,680 --> 00:32:00,160
- Is it pretty?
- Yeah.

363
00:32:01,200 --> 00:32:03,840
You two are really close.

364
00:32:03,920 --> 00:32:06,560
Well, we've known each other forever.

365
00:32:06,640 --> 00:32:07,960
Want to be close with us too?

366
00:32:09,320 --> 00:32:10,240
I'll pass.

367
00:32:11,280 --> 00:32:12,160
Don't kill the mood.

368
00:32:20,240 --> 00:32:22,160
LeeIth says that a lot, doesn't he?

369
00:32:24,440 --> 00:32:26,760
Yeah, but I don't mind.

370
00:32:30,800 --> 00:32:31,760
Hey.

371
00:32:31,840 --> 00:32:35,040
When you're with us,
you can talk about anything.

372
00:32:35,120 --> 00:32:36,480
No holding back. Don't front.

373
00:32:36,560 --> 00:32:37,400
You get me?

374
00:32:41,200 --> 00:32:42,520
I do miss him.

375
00:32:42,600 --> 00:32:44,160
Do you want to make up with him?

376
00:32:47,840 --> 00:32:50,080
Well… I don't know.

377
00:32:56,800 --> 00:32:58,680
Yeah, I do.

378
00:32:58,760 --> 00:33:00,200
If it's possible.

379
00:33:00,840 --> 00:33:02,440
That's it.

380
00:33:02,520 --> 00:33:06,440
First, you need to figure out
how you really feel.

381
00:33:06,520 --> 00:33:09,680
I can tell what you're thinking
just by looking into your eyes.

382
00:33:10,200 --> 00:33:12,120
We're so alike.

383
00:33:12,200 --> 00:33:14,320
You two are both so stubborn.

384
00:33:15,080 --> 00:33:16,600
That hit hard.

385
00:33:17,240 --> 00:33:18,520
You're so good at dealing with

386
00:33:18,600 --> 00:33:19,960
people's problems, but not your own.

387
00:33:20,040 --> 00:33:21,560
That's not true.

388
00:33:21,640 --> 00:33:23,520
Whenever I want you to make up with me,

389
00:33:23,600 --> 00:33:25,000
I've already planned everything.

390
00:33:26,200 --> 00:33:28,520
You never realized
I got you wrapped around my finger.

391
00:33:29,440 --> 00:33:31,560
Hey, did you two forget about me?

392
00:33:31,640 --> 00:33:33,480
See? You forgot your friend.

393
00:33:33,560 --> 00:33:36,320
- Whoops, sorry.
- Sorry.

394
00:33:36,400 --> 00:33:37,440
I'm kidding.

395
00:33:37,520 --> 00:33:39,440
But seriously, thanks, you guys.

396
00:33:39,520 --> 00:33:41,320
I feel a lot better now
that I've talked about it.

397
00:33:41,400 --> 00:33:43,480
If you get the chance, give it a shot.

398
00:33:43,560 --> 00:33:44,800
Or you'll regret it.

399
00:33:47,960 --> 00:33:49,200
Did you tell him that story yet?

400
00:33:49,280 --> 00:33:51,160
About when you confessed
your feelings to me.

401
00:33:51,240 --> 00:33:52,480
Yeah, I did.

402
00:33:52,560 --> 00:33:53,880
How much did you tell him?

403
00:33:53,960 --> 00:33:55,680
Everything.

404
00:33:55,760 --> 00:33:58,400
Did you tell him you cried too?

405
00:33:58,480 --> 00:33:59,360
No.

406
00:33:59,960 --> 00:34:02,720
Back then, Proud cried so hard,

407
00:34:02,800 --> 00:34:05,440
she was bright red
and all her coolness was gone.

408
00:34:05,520 --> 00:34:06,920
Stop gossiping about me already.

409
00:34:07,000 --> 00:34:08,960
My bad. Sorry.

410
00:34:11,760 --> 00:34:13,719
Hey, hey, hey! That's so cute.

411
00:34:27,120 --> 00:34:29,600
4 DAYS BEFORE THE COMPETITION

412
00:34:33,440 --> 00:34:36,480
Lee. Are you going
to watch Putter compete?

413
00:34:38,520 --> 00:34:40,840
I'm busy. Cheer him on for me.

414
00:34:42,040 --> 00:34:43,199
Lee!

415
00:34:44,360 --> 00:34:45,520
Come on, just go.

416
00:34:46,040 --> 00:34:48,360
- Will you?
- I'm busy.

417
00:34:53,320 --> 00:34:54,440
Damn it.

418
00:34:55,040 --> 00:34:56,080
Hey, Bro.

419
00:34:57,200 --> 00:34:58,240
Bro.

420
00:34:58,320 --> 00:34:59,800
Are you going to watch Putter compete?

421
00:35:00,520 --> 00:35:01,360
Let me think about it.

422
00:35:01,440 --> 00:35:02,680
Hey, wait.

423
00:35:03,800 --> 00:35:05,240
Jia's going too.

424
00:35:06,080 --> 00:35:07,240
So?

425
00:35:07,320 --> 00:35:09,000
Well, you two have gotten
pretty close lately,

426
00:35:09,080 --> 00:35:10,440
so I invited him too.

427
00:35:12,920 --> 00:35:16,120
You want me to go because you
want me to make up with Putter, right?

428
00:35:17,480 --> 00:35:18,600
Okay.

429
00:35:18,680 --> 00:35:20,920
I'll be straight with you. Yeah.

430
00:35:21,560 --> 00:35:23,440
But won't that just make things worse?

431
00:35:24,040 --> 00:35:25,520
If he still likes me.

432
00:35:26,120 --> 00:35:27,560
You're pretty confident, huh?

433
00:35:28,080 --> 00:35:29,360
I'm just thinking ahead.

434
00:35:29,440 --> 00:35:32,800
Besides, if Lee sees me,
he'll take it out on me again. Damn it.

435
00:35:32,880 --> 00:35:34,800
Lee isn't going.

436
00:35:37,160 --> 00:35:38,440
Yeah, I'll think about it.

437
00:35:43,960 --> 00:35:44,840
Seriously…

438
00:35:44,920 --> 00:35:46,320
You couldn't do it?

439
00:35:46,400 --> 00:35:48,160
I've got nothing left to say.

440
00:35:49,360 --> 00:35:55,000
Well, Proud and Summer said
Putter's still worried about you guys.

441
00:35:55,080 --> 00:35:58,960
If… you two…
could work things out, that'd be nice.

442
00:35:59,040 --> 00:36:01,480
Since when was that my responsibility?

443
00:36:02,600 --> 00:36:05,080
They said if the club has fewer
than six members,

444
00:36:05,160 --> 00:36:06,440
it's definitely getting shut down.

445
00:36:07,680 --> 00:36:08,960
Say bye-bye to the room.

446
00:36:13,360 --> 00:36:14,840
- Good luck.
- Good luck.

447
00:36:19,720 --> 00:36:22,440
If not for our friendship,
then I'll do it for the club.

448
00:36:29,480 --> 00:36:30,640
<i>Prepare Plan B.</i>

449
00:36:31,880 --> 00:36:34,640
<i>If we can't do it the easy way,</i>
<i>we'll have to use another tactic.</i>

450
00:36:36,640 --> 00:36:37,840
<i>Tactic?</i>

451
00:36:59,840 --> 00:37:01,440
- What the hell is this?
- Grab him.

452
00:37:01,520 --> 00:37:03,160
- Let me go!
- Stay still.

453
00:37:03,240 --> 00:37:05,880
- Get over here.
- Hey, hey, hey!

454
00:37:05,960 --> 00:37:08,800
- Stop struggling! Stop struggling!
- Damn it, I'm heavy!

455
00:37:08,880 --> 00:37:10,080
Turn him around! Turn him around!

456
00:37:10,160 --> 00:37:12,480
- Go, go!
- Past the chair! Past the chair!

457
00:37:12,560 --> 00:37:13,720
- Yeah, that's it!
- What the hell is this?

458
00:37:13,800 --> 00:37:15,680
- Hold him down! Hold him down!
- Grab him! Grab him!

459
00:37:15,760 --> 00:37:17,080
- Stop struggling!
- Let me go!

460
00:37:17,160 --> 00:37:18,360
This is your Plan B? Your "tactic"?

461
00:37:18,440 --> 00:37:20,360
Yeah. By "tactic," I mean brute force.

462
00:37:21,120 --> 00:37:22,520
- Damn it!
- Stay still!

463
00:37:23,360 --> 00:37:25,240
We've already talked
things through with Indy.

464
00:37:25,320 --> 00:37:26,280
You're the only one left.

465
00:37:26,360 --> 00:37:27,880
Yeah, and you're about to compete.

466
00:37:27,960 --> 00:37:29,160
So you won't have any regrets.

467
00:37:29,240 --> 00:37:30,200
Just get it over with, okay?

468
00:37:30,280 --> 00:37:32,560
- Do you get it?
- Do you get it?

469
00:37:33,600 --> 00:37:34,680
- Go.
- Go, go, go!

470
00:37:35,280 --> 00:37:37,200
- Damn it! I can't get my shirt off!
- Hurry up!

471
00:37:37,280 --> 00:37:38,480
Come on! Come on!

472
00:37:39,000 --> 00:37:40,400
You bunch of kidnappers.

473
00:37:44,560 --> 00:37:46,160
Don't you think they're overdoing it?

474
00:37:47,200 --> 00:37:48,440
Big time.

475
00:37:56,080 --> 00:37:57,440
Here, let me fix it for you.

476
00:38:24,360 --> 00:38:25,560
Thanks.

477
00:38:35,920 --> 00:38:37,400
I'm sorry too, Putter.

478
00:38:38,280 --> 00:38:41,280
That day, I… didn't mean it.

479
00:38:43,720 --> 00:38:45,440
I wasn't that mad at you anyway.

480
00:38:51,760 --> 00:38:52,880
And…

481
00:38:55,000 --> 00:38:56,320
what about your other feelings?

482
00:39:00,360 --> 00:39:01,400
Well…

483
00:39:01,920 --> 00:39:03,360
I did have feelings for you.

484
00:39:12,120 --> 00:39:13,400
Crap, sorry. Are you okay?

485
00:39:13,480 --> 00:39:16,040
I'm fine. It's all good. See you around.

486
00:39:18,560 --> 00:39:22,040
<i>Back then, I fell for your kindness.</i>

487
00:39:24,360 --> 00:39:25,360
<i>Lee…</i>

488
00:39:33,240 --> 00:39:34,520
<i>My heart was really racing.</i>

489
00:39:35,040 --> 00:39:36,560
<i>I thought you were going</i>
<i>to ask for my Instagram.</i>

490
00:39:46,040 --> 00:39:49,160
Even though I knew you already liked Faye,

491
00:39:49,920 --> 00:39:51,960
my feelings had already taken over.

492
00:39:59,320 --> 00:40:01,760
So… what about now?

493
00:40:11,120 --> 00:40:12,920
I… don't have feelings for you anymore.

494
00:40:13,480 --> 00:40:14,600
So you can relax.

495
00:40:15,440 --> 00:40:17,200
I see you as 100% a friend.

496
00:40:24,520 --> 00:40:25,840
It's just…

497
00:40:26,640 --> 00:40:28,120
I'm okay now, but…

498
00:40:28,640 --> 00:40:30,200
I was afraid you'd feel uncomfortable.

499
00:40:31,440 --> 00:40:32,480
Because…

500
00:40:33,240 --> 00:40:36,120
I understand what it's like to have
feelings for someone,

501
00:40:37,080 --> 00:40:38,440
and it feels like you're given hope.

502
00:40:39,800 --> 00:40:40,960
Damn… you know how that feels?

503
00:40:42,840 --> 00:40:43,960
Shit.

504
00:40:44,800 --> 00:40:46,160
Talking about this really gets to me.

505
00:40:47,840 --> 00:40:50,280
So, there's nothing
between us anymore, right?

506
00:40:50,800 --> 00:40:52,120
We've cleared things up.

507
00:40:53,240 --> 00:40:54,720
Now it's just your friend.

508
00:40:58,240 --> 00:40:59,600
Just give him some time.

509
00:41:00,120 --> 00:41:03,280
That idiot…
he takes everything way too far.

510
00:41:03,360 --> 00:41:05,040
He'll calm down eventually.

511
00:41:10,640 --> 00:41:11,800
Thanks.

512
00:41:16,120 --> 00:41:19,400
I'm sorry for being so immature.

513
00:41:23,160 --> 00:41:24,280
Come on.

514
00:41:25,960 --> 00:41:27,880
Uh… you guys are done talking, right?

515
00:41:27,960 --> 00:41:29,520
No one's kissing or anything, right?

516
00:41:29,600 --> 00:41:31,160
We were just about to come in.

517
00:41:31,760 --> 00:41:33,200
Yeah, we're good.

518
00:41:33,280 --> 00:41:34,200
Come on in.

519
00:41:38,320 --> 00:41:39,760
- You guys are the best!
- The best!

520
00:41:39,840 --> 00:41:41,560
You guys are the best!

521
00:41:41,640 --> 00:41:43,960
You idiot! I told you we're friends.

522
00:41:46,360 --> 00:41:47,560
Okay, okay.

523
00:41:48,560 --> 00:41:50,320
Now you can focus on your tournament
with peace of mind, buddy.

524
00:41:52,720 --> 00:41:54,640
All of us…

525
00:41:54,720 --> 00:41:55,760
We'll talk to him ourselves.

526
00:41:58,040 --> 00:41:59,920
I'll drag that idiot here if I have to.

527
00:42:01,160 --> 00:42:02,240
You don't have to force him.

528
00:42:02,760 --> 00:42:03,640
I'm okay.

529
00:42:04,840 --> 00:42:07,520
Everyone, let's cheer for Putter!

530
